[00:00.00]Many people always want to improve their English quickly in a short time.|很多人总想在短时间内快速提高英语。
[00:04.90]They memorize hundreds of words today, do countless exercises tomorrow, and start learning difficult grammar the next day.|他们今天背几百个单词，明天做无数道练习，后天又开始啃难懂的语法。
[00:13.96]It may look like hard work, but in fact, they are only anxiously chasing progress.|看起来像是在努力，其实只是在焦虑地追赶进度。
[00:21.46]Language learning is never a sprint.|语言学习从来不是短跑。
[00:23.96]It is a long journey that requires patience and steady effort.|它是一段漫长的旅程，需要耐心和稳定的付出。
[00:28.14]People who truly learn English well are usually not the fastest learners, but those who are willing to stay calm and keep going step by step.|真正把英语学好的人，往往不是学得最快的，而是愿意沉住气、一步一步往前走的人。
[00:39.86]Trying to learn English too quickly will never bring good results.|想太快学会英语，永远不会有好结果。
[00:45.12]Being greedy for more and faster progress will only leave you with nothing in the end.|贪多求快，最后只会一无所获。
[00:51.84]Real improvement always comes from daily accumulation.|真正的进步，永远来自每天的积累。
[00:55.16]There is no need to blindly rush your progress.|没有必要盲目赶进度。
[00:59.52]Slow down and fully understand every piece of knowledge.|慢下来，把每一个知识点都彻底弄懂。
[01:03.58]Build a strong foundation and move forward steadily.|打好扎实的基础，稳稳地往前走。
[01:07.96]Calm and steady learning is far more valuable than impatiently doing endless exercises.|沉静而扎实的学习，远比焦躁地刷无穷无尽的题更有价值。
[01:15.58]Stay patient, keep learning little by little, and persist for a long time.|保持耐心，一点一点地学，长期坚持下去。
[01:21.48]Then your English ability will naturally improve step by step.|你的英语水平自然会一步一步提升。
